<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brigid (goddess)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brigid is a goddess of early Irish mythology, a daughter of the Dagda associated with poetry, healing and smithcraft. Her feast fell at Imbolc, the start of spring. Many of her attributes were later linked with Saint Brigid of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kildare">Kildare</a>, and scholars often compare her with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brigantia">Brigantia</a>, the goddess of the British Brigantes.</p></div>
